No accessibility node under an invisible element (GPUI patch for docs/plans/20261031-e2e-ui-and-coverage.md Task 7):
GPUI paints nothing of an element whose style is `Visibility::Hidden` (`.invisible()`), yet prepaints its children,
which published their AccessKit nodes all the same, so assistive technology found controls nobody could see (a hidden
HTML overlay page's strip, laid out where it would show, kept its Hide button in the tree on AT-SPI and UIA alike).
A hidden div now prepaints its children with node publication held off (`A11y::hidden`, checked by
`A11y::publishes` where an element pushes its node); the invisible element's own node, pushed before its style is
known, stays. An upstream candidate (Zed).
For its regression test (ngterm-gpui's chrome::button tests; gpui-pre's own lib tests do not build from the crates.io
archive), the test window keeps the accessibility callbacks GPUI connects and the tree updates it sends, and
`VisualTestContext::activate_a11y` connects assistive technology, `VisualTestContext::a11y_tree_update` reads the last
update; a test that does not activate it runs as before.
scripts/vendor-gpui.sh applies this after 0005.

